#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171739 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "104ad420-9a16-51b9-bfc5-16080b22fd49" :question/math-academy-id "e-5108" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{3} \\choose {\\color{blue}2}},$ we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $\\color{red}3$ and position $\\color{blue}2$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\ ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} = 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171740 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Relationship Between the Rows of Pascal's Triangle in Terms of Binomial Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "587f0594-4911-5ad7-9f1a-bd33cfbad3fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5109" :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{\\left[ \\phantom{3 \\choose 3}\\right]}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\displaystyle{\\color{red}{4} \\choose {\\color{blue}3}},$ we need to find the number that is located in row $\\color{red}4$ and position $\\color{blue}3$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important:** Remember that when counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero!\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3}$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{4 \\choose 3} = \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 2} + \\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\displaystyle{3 \\choose 3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171741 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "9f9efb07-33a0-5a28-8eef-656a3c00a200" :question/math-academy-id "e-5231" :question/problem "Determine the value of $\\displaystyle{5 \\choose 4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial coefficient $\\displaystyle{n \\choose r}$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{n \\choose r} = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,  r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n = 5$ and $r = 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{5}{4}) & =\\frac{5!}{(5-4)!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 4!}{1!\\cdot 4!} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{4!}}{1\\cdot \\cancel{4!}} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b754b8b-4181-58d1-aec1-0217d8b7a23d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282421} {:answer/id #uuid "92e129af-4eb5-5011-9457-7da327ae421b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282422} {:answer/id #uuid "73a06fde-a74c-5b0b-89d7-b7eeb00f268c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282423} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd38594-9c75-5d19-ad00-5ca0efa8186c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282424} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0ac021-c519-543b-906b-d44e3ec7d76c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d0ac021-c519-543b-906b-d44e3ec7d76c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282425} :answer-field/id #uuid "748d3607-8524-59db-8c0e-6bffaf0b4f72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d8a60a5-1247-5261-b9c3-a74b9b06271f" :question/math-academy-id "q-112325" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{3}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $(\\frac{3}{3}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $3$ and position $3$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $3$ and position $3$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 4 &  & 6 &  & 4 &  & 1 \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\frac{3}{3})=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a959cfb-a279-5b7e-ba5c-39eed2dcf9e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282428} {:answer/id #uuid "d713d392-a1ce-5b66-8699-e60548e012ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282429} {:answer/id #uuid "96900aff-da77-5dba-91a9-c503cd11e0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282430} {:answer/id #uuid "790b7333-21c6-5ce6-b5dd-017d93b8c0d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282431} {:answer/id #uuid "d04e6084-e2b4-56d8-9e4e-724bf2d7b15b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d713d392-a1ce-5b66-8699-e60548e012ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282429} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd09d3ce-e84d-5a04-ba13-312d64cdcd4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4ca1679-3b0d-5d85-8df3-e4d140abafd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-112328" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{2}{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $(\\frac{2}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $2$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $2$ and position $1$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\frac{2}{1})=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "be11193b-a241-5812-a1c1-54d233ae9ddd" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of a Binomial Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c259f71b-0798-5c86-8c9a-1cceda46ec59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282435} {:answer/id #uuid "1b85e886-e3b3-5901-be12-185bdf793b58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282436} {:answer/id #uuid "8834803e-48c9-57cb-a0a5-0f987ac95684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282437} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc1acbd-a8cb-5b2f-a5d6-2c909d0b779d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282438} {:answer/id #uuid "9712dad4-8889-5a45-8444-887649039016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8834803e-48c9-57cb-a0a5-0f987ac95684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282437} :answer-field/id #uuid "07b2fff0-6a41-5ed9-b5ac-acb1cf6c7508" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5deb48f3-1beb-5d95-8f36-d7d4c47e7bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-112329" :question/problem "Use Pascal's triangle to determine the value of $(\\frac{6}{1}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the value of $(\\frac{6}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $6$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe value located in row $6$ and position $1$ is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 2 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  &  & 1 &  & 3 &  & 3 &  & 1 \\\\  &  &  & 1 &  & 4 &  & 6 &  & 4 &  & 1 \\\\  &  & 1 &  & 5 &  & 10 &  & 10 &  & 5 &  & 1 \\\\  & 1 &  & 6 &  & 15 &  & 20 &  & 15 &  & 6 &  & 1 \\\\ ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(\\frac{6}{1})=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Relationship Between the Rows of Pascal's Triangle in Terms of Binomial Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2054c014-3ab0-5209-96f7-44707cb4e4a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{0}{0})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282442} {:answer/id #uuid "37daef10-4236-5d97-bfaf-8aecfd86c6f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282443} {:answer/id #uuid "20f34332-d954-51f4-811f-64152ab1e2f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282444} {:answer/id #uuid "5edce38a-13a4-5113-b5c5-6a7b6cff5222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{2}{0})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282445} {:answer/id #uuid "bed225b9-b725-52e6-8f7a-8a74e4bac960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bed225b9-b725-52e6-8f7a-8a74e4bac960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{1}{1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282446} :answer-field/id #uuid "669cc06d-02cb-58e4-b270-c99b4929483a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "239de6c5-ea8b-5080-a1b4-6a809e8010bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-113604" :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{2}{1})=(\\frac{1}{0})+[]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\frac{2}{1}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $2$ and position $1$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{2}{1})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{2}{1})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{2}{1})=(\\frac{1}{0})+(\\frac{1}{1})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{1}{1}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c976b6a-4523-51e1-a243-27aa8937db25" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Relationship Between the Rows of Pascal's Triangle in Terms of Binomial Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ffe23f-d4c4-5529-9e6c-1030767cd140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{4}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282449} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f26be9-f5c6-53a0-988e-6df3a1869488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{6}{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282450} {:answer/id #uuid "18408428-cb99-5929-abda-1f295e8b69e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282451} {:answer/id #uuid "be9c16a6-f6b7-57f4-8fd8-34c27b5cb6b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{4}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282452} {:answer/id #uuid "5105df09-2e97-5c1c-a3d5-4da5cb0adc61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{6}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18408428-cb99-5929-abda-1f295e8b69e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282451} :answer-field/id #uuid "48239091-3dc1-5d58-86b9-0eac7e555108" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282448}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a4f4639c-e80e-5af7-837b-1a24cc1a33b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113608" :question/problem "Which expression is missing in the following equation?\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{5})=[]+(\\frac{5}{5})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find $(\\frac{6}{5}),$ we need to find the number that is located in row $6$ and position $5$ of Pascal's triangle. \n\n**Important**: When counting the rows and positions in Pascal's triangle, we always start counting from zero! Remember:\n\n- The top row of Pascal's triangle is row $0.$\n\n- The first position of each row (the one of the left) is position number $0.$\n\nThe location of $(\\frac{6}{5})$ in Pascal's triangle is highlighted below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{0}{0}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{1}{0}) &  & (\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{2}{0}) &  & (\\frac{2}{1}) &  & (\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  &  &  &  &  & (\\frac{3}{0}) &  & (\\frac{3}{1}) &  & (\\frac{3}{2}) &  & (\\frac{3}{3}) \\\\  &  &  &  & (\\frac{4}{0}) &  & (\\frac{4}{1}) &  & (\\frac{4}{2}) &  & (\\frac{4}{3}) &  & (\\frac{4}{4}) \\\\  &  &  & (\\frac{5}{0}) &  & (\\frac{5}{1}) &  & (\\frac{5}{2}) &  & (\\frac{5}{3}) &  & (\\frac{5}{4}) &  & (\\frac{5}{5}) \\\\  &  & (\\frac{6}{0}) &  & (\\frac{6}{1}) &  & (\\frac{6}{2}) &  & (\\frac{6}{3}) &  & (\\frac{6}{4}) &  & (\\frac{6}{5}) &  & (\\frac{6}{6}) \\\\  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮ &  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $(\\frac{6}{5})$ is the sum of the two closest numbers located in the previous row. So,\n\n$$\n(\\frac{6}{5})=(\\frac{5}{4})+(\\frac{5}{5})\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $(\\frac{5}{4}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb4ec934-95fd-57ba-931e-73fadb7310f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282456} {:answer/id #uuid "55d37008-3ded-55ad-9b46-a0336f626e59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282457} {:answer/id #uuid "145b8110-f8c7-5a72-a618-8f189015cd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282458} {:answer/id #uuid "808587d7-c3b5-51f0-9f11-cfbce73229e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282459} {:answer/id #uuid "3925c0be-3ce4-5582-a3ae-3d6e18a0403d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "145b8110-f8c7-5a72-a618-8f189015cd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282458} :answer-field/id #uuid "833d3b40-41e0-5da0-9986-f9afddf1b372" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b955a904-102b-509c-b6fe-26db40c4d90a" :question/math-academy-id "q-113613" :question/problem "Determine the value of $(\\frac{8}{5}).$" :question/worked-solution "The binomial coefficient $(\\frac{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\frac{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=8$ and $r=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{8}{5}) & =\\frac{8!}{(8-5)!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{3!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{6\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot \\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{\\cancel{6}\\cdot \\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5c108c0-f32a-5725-af3b-c3e747da09f2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Binomial Coefficients Using the Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf54f00-ebd8-5e93-91c7-02b25552e46c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282463} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6ff311-9f77-576f-ad6c-97fceaf47e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282464} {:answer/id #uuid "3b7a4088-c748-5998-b6fd-e38b5245f68c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186